// What the combat tuner may change. Each entry is one number the search moves:
//   name     how the run's tables call it
//   path     where it lives: a content file, then a dotted path of keys (or array indexes) to a
//            number already in that file, e.g. "species.json:species.Wolf.boldness"
//   paths    instead of path: several numbers that move together (they start at the first one's value)
//   min/max  the range searched; today's value must lie inside it (the search starts there)
//   log      search on a log scale (for multipliers and damages that span orders of magnitude)
//   integer  round to a whole number (the table reads an int)
//   note     why it is here, or what to watch
// To tune a new constant, put it in a content table and add an entry here: no tool code changes.
// Every number below is in data today; combat constants still in code are not tuned yet.
